I haven't seen any of these posted so I will assume they are unknown.

This is for the PC version of NH3.0pl7 (my compilation with all options)

1) You start eating food, it is rotten, you stop eating for some reason,
   you resume eating, it tastes delicious.

2) Using ' ' (a space only) as a player name, [don't ask me why he does it],
   This name will be accepted and will be mapped to '_' when used for save
   files.  However when a player with that name enters the score list, it
   will cause truncation in later games since nethack goes by a blank to
   indicate end-of-data.

3) When the scorelist has many scores for the same person (but different
   characters), the display will overflow with all of that player's entries.
   Thus all of the top 10 are missed.

4) You are blind, you dip your long sword into the fountain for the magic
   treatment, you _see_ a murky hand rise out of the depths.


I have checked that 2 is not in the UNIX version.

